rants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"American (New), Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Southern","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"yY3kq6_2m1FyY9MgaiHgoQ","review_id":"6UjGlL54ODrM8yhTVEEjnQ","date":"2010-11-12T19:59:56","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9401673078536987,"text_excerpt":"My new go to place for out of towners. I've been dying to go here for years and finally went for a friend's birthday. Everyone loved what they ordered. The fried green tomato shrimp remoulade poboy was amazing. The onion rings were nice and flaky as well. As a birthday treat, the waiter brought out 3 desserts, which was plenty for the 8 of us to share. The desserts were the famous fried poboy bread pudding, peanut butter pie, and pecan pie. Now, I am not the biggest bread pudding fan, but man, that thing was amazing! Nice and flaky on the outside, topped with powder sugar; gooey on the inside. YUMMY went back recently with 7 people who live/have lived in the city, but have never tried ye ..."},{"business_id":"yY3kq6_2m1FyY9MgaiHgoQ","review_id":"ewN7lerW-75C-zylBV_Rxg","date":"2019-10-21T18:03:20","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9366636276245117,"text_excerpt":"This past weekend was at least the 3rd (probably 4th) time I've come here for dinner, and at least the 3rd (probably 4th) time I've really, really enjoyed the food and service. This time, I had the special which was red snapper with crab meat, along with honey glazed shrimp and a purple sweet potato and andouille \"hash\". It was much more than I could finish, but every single part of the meal was fantastic. (we actually took home leftovers of the potato/andouille base and made an amazing fried egg breakfast the next day) My date had the duck salad appetizer and brussels sprouts side dish as her meal, and loved them. Oh, and their seafood gumbo was delicious. On a previous trip, I had the l..."},{"business_id":"yY3kq6_2m1FyY9MgaiHgoQ","review_id":"nssW1-rpyQnPdBfk6YB-JA","date":"2014-08-13T18:43:57","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9353470802307129,"text_excerpt":"I made my first visit to YOCI last night with my girlfriend and another couple and I will DEFINITELY be back. So good! Girlfriend knows some of the chefs, who hooked us up with a comped appetizer and dessert, making the meal that much better. The grilled flatbread app featured oxtail and was delicious. The table also shared some fried oysters (topped with blue cheese!) and BBQ shrimp. Both fantastic. The sauce accompanying the shrimp was thick, creamy, and not to be wasted. Good thing it was served with some toasty French bread for dipping. For my main course I had the hamburger steak, which was topped with sauteed onions and brown gravy. Huge portion so I've got some left over for dinner..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"yY3kq6_2m1FyY9MgaiHgoQ","photo_id":"Mq7hzCIXYs_-gw7sBL_iuA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/Mq7hzCIXYs_-gw7sBL_iuA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9234872460365295},{"business_id":"yY3kq6_2m1FyY9MgaiHgoQ","photo_id":"bcjGBOwaMmIHh_TVheNlaA","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/bcjGBOwaMmIHh_TVheNlaA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8439069986343384},{"business_id":"yY3kq6_2m1FyY